# KnowledgeHub AI Workflow

- Read `AGENTS.md` before making significant changes.
- Work in small tasks requiring approximately 60-90 minutes.
- Inspect existing code before editing it.
- Explain the proposed change before implementation.
- Add meaningful comments for non-obvious logic.
- Do not introduce databases, frameworks, infrastructure, or abstractions
  unless the current feature needs them.
- Keep API, service, schema, and configuration responsibilities separate.
- Never claim that tests passed unless they were actually executed.
- Do not automatically commit or push changes.
- When the user invokes `/end-session`, update project documentation based
  only on the actual repository changes.
